{"name":"Devil’s Grass","hex":"#44aa55","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"devil","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["The chief devil; Satan."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["An evil creature, the objectification of a hostile and destructive force.","A man with red or orange skin and a pair of horns on his head, a pointed goatee, and a long tail, who carries a pitchfork, represents evil, and is portrayed to children as a boogeyman who punishes bad behavior."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/devil"},{"term":"grass","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Any plant of the family Poaceae, characterized by leaves that arise from nodes in the stem and leaf bases that wrap around the stem, especially those grown as ground cover rather than for grain.","Any of the various plants that are not in the family Poaceae that resemble grasses."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To lay out on the grass; to knock down (an opponent etc.).","To act as a grass or informer, to betray; to report on (criminals etc) to the authorities."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/grass"}],"entries":[{"title":"Grass","blocks":[{"text":"Grass refers to various families of plants. The three major families of grasslike plants are true grasses (Poaceae), sedges (Cyperaceae), and rushes (Juncaceae). Lawns and pasturelands are typically composed of true grasses, five of which cover 46% of the world's arable land: rice, wheat, maize, barley, and sugar cane."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/77/Poa_annua.jpg/330px-Poa_annua.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Grass"},{"title":"Devil","blocks":[{"text":"The devil is a mythical personification of evil as conceived in various cultures and religious traditions. It is seen as the objectification of a hostile and destructive force. Jeffrey Burton Russell states that the different conceptions of the Devil can be summed up as 1. a principle of evil independent from God, 2. an aspect of God, 3. a created being turning evil or 4. a symbol of human evil."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/77/022_devil_representation.JPG/330px-022_devil_representation.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Devil"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/50/BlueAngel.png/120px-BlueAngel.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/50/BlueAngel.png/250px-BlueAngel.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/50/BlueAngel.png/120px-BlueAngel.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Excerpt of a Byzantine-Mosaic-Image. A blue angel, probably representing the Devil, standing before goats. Early 6th century.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ABlueAngel.png"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/ae/Nuremberg_chronicles_-_Devil_and_Woman_on_Horseback_%28CLXXXIXv%29.jpg/500px-Nuremberg_chronicles_-_Devil_and_Woman_on_Horseback_%28CLXXXIXv%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/ae/Nuremberg_chronicles_-_Devil_and_Woman_on_Horseback_%28CLXXXIXv%29.jpg/1280px-Nuremberg_chronicles_-_Devil_and_Woman_on_Horseback_%28CLXXXIXv%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/ae/Nuremberg_chronicles_-_Devil_and_Woman_on_Horseback_%28CLXXXIXv%29.jpg/500px-Nuremberg_chronicles_-_Devil_and_Woman_on_Horseback_%28CLXXXIXv%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"The Dev